# Real bin/fm-bootstrap.sh from the gate worktree, lab home $LAB (bin/fm-lab-home.sh create), run on macOS with the WSL marker
# WSL_DISTRO_NAME set and stand-ins for the Windows side under $LAB/winside/bin (wslinfo, cmd.exe, wslpath -> $LAB/winside/Users/fm)
## Scenario: WSL, projects directory on the Windows drive

### WSL, FM projects at /mnt/c/Users/fm/projects
$ WSL_DISTRO_NAME=Ubuntu-24.04 FM_PROJECTS_OVERRIDE=/mnt/c/Users/fm/projects PATH=$LAB/winside/bin:$PATH bin/fm-bootstrap.sh   (TOOLCHAIN_DRIFT lines from the host toolchain filtered)
HOST_ENV: WSL: /mnt/c/Users/fm/projects is on the Windows drive - move it under the Linux home (~); git, file watching and file permissions are slow or broken under /mnt/
[took 13s]

### Adversarial: /mnt/wsl is not a drive letter
$ WSL_DISTRO_NAME=Ubuntu-24.04 FM_PROJECTS_OVERRIDE=/mnt/wsl/projects PATH=$LAB/winside/bin:$PATH bin/fm-bootstrap.sh   (TOOLCHAIN_DRIFT lines from the host toolchain filtered)
(no output)
[took 18s]

### Adversarial: same /mnt/c path but not inside WSL
$ FM_PROJECTS_OVERRIDE=/mnt/c/Users/fm/projects PATH=$LAB/winside/bin:$PATH bin/fm-bootstrap.sh   (TOOLCHAIN_DRIFT lines from the host toolchain filtered)
