## Scenario: WSL, localhost forwarding off in .wslconfig

.wslconfig:
  [wsl2]
  memory=8GB
  localhostForwarding = False

### WSL, NAT networking, localhostForwarding=False
$ WSL_DISTRO_NAME=Ubuntu-24.04 PATH=$LAB/winside/bin:$PATH bin/fm-bootstrap.sh   (TOOLCHAIN_DRIFT lines from the host toolchain filtered)
HOST_ENV: WSL: localhost forwarding is off in $LAB/winside/Users/fm/.wslconfig, so review boards and dev servers will not open in the Windows browser - set networkingMode=mirrored under [wsl2] there, then run wsl --shutdown from Windows (ONBOARDING-windows.md)
[took 12s]

### WSL, mirrored networking (wslinfo reports mirrored)
$ WSL_DISTRO_NAME=Ubuntu-24.04 FAKE_WSL_MODE=mirrored PATH=$LAB/winside/bin:$PATH bin/fm-bootstrap.sh   (TOOLCHAIN_DRIFT lines from the host toolchain filtered)
(no output)
[took 9s]

.wslconfig:
  [wsl2]
  networkingMode=mirrored
  memory=8GB

### WSL, recommended .wslconfig from ONBOARDING-windows.md
$ WSL_DISTRO_NAME=Ubuntu-24.04 FAKE_WSL_MODE=mirrored PATH=$LAB/winside/bin:$PATH bin/fm-bootstrap.sh   (TOOLCHAIN_DRIFT lines from the host toolchain filtered)
(no output)
[took 5s]

